  "help": {
    "navtitle": "FAQ",
    "detailTitle": "",
    "question1": "What is ORich?",
    "question2": "About the products?",
    "question3": "Rule",
    "question4": "How is the lucky code generated?",
    "question5": "Delivery and logistics",
    "question6": "About fund withdrawals",
    "question1_1": "1. Product selection",
    "question1_2": "2. Payment",
    "question1_3": "3. Winner revealing",
    "question1_4": "Note:",
    "question1_5": "4. Purchase sharing",
    "question3_1": "Mode 1",
    "question3_2": "Mode 2",
    "answer1": "Browse products and tap \"Join\".",
    "answer2": "Make the payment through an online payment platform to get a \"lucky number\". You can buy shares of one product multiple times or multiple shares of a product at once. The more \"lucky numbers\" you buy, the greater your chance of winning the product.",
    "answer3": "When the full complement of participants is achieved, the draw starts, and the winner is revealed. ORich will notify you via SMS or in-app notice.",
    "answer4": "1) After the winner of a product is revealed, promptly log in and complete your profile. We need accurate details to arrange shipment.",
    "answer5": "2) No refunds for products that have been revealed.",
    "answer6": "Answer: All products on ORich are supplied by local suppliers. We have good partnerships with platforms such as Flipkart and Amazon, guaranteeing product quality.",
    "answer7": "Each product is equally divided into multiple \"shares\", and each share has a lucky code.\n\t\t\t\tYou can buy shares of one product multiple times, or buy multiple pieces of a product at once.\n\t\t\t\tWhen all the \"equal pieces\" are sold, the winning \"lucky code\" is generated. The holder of this \"lucky number\" wins the product.",
    "answer8": "We have strict rules for generating the lucky code to ensure fairness and transparency.\n\t\t\t\tThe system will first select all purchase records of this product before the time of the final purchase.\n\t\t\t\tThen lists the times of these purchase records in hour, minute, second, and millisecond format.\n\t\t\t\tThe numbers are summed and divided by the total number of shares to obtain a remainder. The \"lucky code\" is set equal to the remainder plus 1000001.",
    "answer9": "Products are delivered by our partners.",
    "answerx": "After a withdrawal is initiated, funds will be transferred to your account in two working days or less.",
    "answer11": "Share photos of your product, or even yourself, with your comments, to spread your happiness.",
    "answer12": "In this mode, the “product” is a cash reward, and there are multiple winners: one first prize winner, xx second prize winners, xx third prize winners, and xx fourth prize winners. The win rate is about 30% of the total number of \"shares\", and each share has a lucky number. For example, the prize could be a 50,000-rupee cash prize, with 500 shares, each costing 100 rupees. You can buy several shares one by one, or buy multiple shares at once.\n\t\t\t\tWhen all \"shares\" of a product have been sold, the winning \"lucky number\" is generated. The holder of this lucky number wins the first prize. Holders of numbers that are 1-4 less or greater than the lucky number win the second prize. Holders of numbers that are 5-9 less or greater than the lucky number win the third prize. Simliar rules also apply for other prizes.\n\t\t\t\t"
  },
